      "title": "University Assistant (PhD position)",
      "description": "University Assistant (PhD position) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (PhD position) Start date/duration: as soon as possible for 4 years Administrative unit: Department of Ecology Extent of employment: 20 hours per week; will be increased to 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed Job Description: Your responsibilities: Complete dissertation in the field of Landscape ecology Independent and collaborative research in the field of landscape ecology, focusing on spatial processes, ecological legacies or human-environment interactions Development of an independent PhD project and leading scientific publications in international peer-reviewed journals Conducting spatial and environmental data analyses Participation in interdisciplinary and administrative tasks of the research group and the Institute Continued education and professional development Independent teaching Your profile: Completed Master’s, Magister or Diplom degree (or equivalent) in ecology, geography, remote sensing, landscape ecology or a related field A strong interest in landscape ecology, long-term land-use change and human-environment interactions Experience in handling large datasets, technical affinity and a willingness to work with spatial and quantitative research methods would be an advantage An interest in scientific publishing and the motivation to build an international publication profile Very good written and spoken English A basic knowledge of German would be an advantage, along with a willingness to develop your German language skills Ability to work as part of a team, ability to work independently and strong communication skills Please include a two-page description of your proposed PhD project Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/BIO-15884 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#dissertationsstellen Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for 20 hours per week amounts to € 1.888 per month (14 times)*. The salary will be increased to € 2.832 for 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed and sent to the Personnel Department. The salary will be higher if you have worked in a similar position before. * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 11.11.2026 stating the code BIO-15884 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Catalina Munteanu Phone: +4351250751629 Email: Catalina-Mihaela.Munteanu@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
    },
    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=15978": {
      "title": "University Assistant (PhD position)",
      "description": "University Assistant (PhD position) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (PhD position) Start date/duration: as soon as possible for 4 years Administrative unit: Department of Statistics Extent of employment: 20 hours per week; will be increased to 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed Job Description: Your responsibilities: PhD thesis in the field of statistics Independent research in the field of probabilistic modelling, statistical inference and machine learning, with potential applications to practical problems Independent teaching Supporting research work, participation in research projects, and assistance with teaching and examination duties Training and professional development Administrative duties Your profile: A relevant completed Master, Magister or Diplom degree in the fields of statistics, data science, mathematics or economics, with a specialisation in statistics or econometrics Very good knowledge of mathematics, particularly probability theory and statistics Proven programming experience in a high-level programming language (particularly R or Python) Excellent command of English, excellent command of German is a plus Teamwork and communication skills Please include with your application a comprising a covering letter, CV and academic transcripts and a written outline of your proposed dissertation topic (approx. 1 page) Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/VWL-15978 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#dissertationsstellen Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for 20 hours per week amounts to € 1.888 per month (14 times)*. The salary will be increased to € 2.832 for 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed and sent to the Personnel Department. The salary will be higher if you have worked in a similar position before. * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 11.11.2026 stating the code VWL-15978 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Univ.-Prof. Dr. Nikolaus Umlauf Email: Nikolaus.Umlauf@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
