    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=16023": {
      "title": "Studentische Mitarbeit in Forschung und Verwaltung",
      "description": "Studentische Mitarbeit in Forschung und Verwaltung Suche Quicklinks Navigation Karriereportal Stellenangebote / Bewerben Meine Bewerbungen Mein Qualifikationsprofil Meine Dokumente Meine Daten Meine Zugangsdaten Hilfe Kontakt Login Zurück PDF Ausgabe Online bewerben Studentische Mitarbeit in Forschung und Verwaltung Beginn/Dauer: ehest möglich auf 4 Jahre Organisationseinheit: Italienisches Recht, Standort Innsbruck Beschäftigungsausmaß: 10 Stunden/Woche Ihre Aufgaben: Mitarbeit an wissenschaftlichen Projekten im Bereich Italienisches Verfassungsrecht Mithilfe bei der Betreuung von Studierenden Mitarbeit in der Verwaltung insbesondere bei der Betreuung der Bibliothek für Italienisches öffentliches Recht Ihr Profil: Laufendes Studium (Bachelor/Diplom/Master) der Rechtswissenschaften Solide Kenntnisse im Italienischen Verfassungsrecht und Interesse für das Italienische Verfassungs- und Autonomierecht Sehr gute Kenntnis der Sprachen Deutsch und Italienisch Teamfähigkeit, Zuverlässigkeit, Einsatzbereitschaft, Bereitschaft zum eigenständigen Arbeiten Erwünscht: Laufendes integriertes Diplomstudium Italienisches Recht, Erfahrung mit Bibliotheksarbeit, gute Englischkenntnisse Die Beschreibung der mit dieser Stelle verbundenen Aufgaben und Anforderungen finden Sie unter: https://www.uibk.ac.at/de/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#studentische-mitarbeiterinnen Unser Angebot: Bei uns erwarten Sie spannende Aufgaben, flexible Arbeitszeiten, ein familienfreundliches Arbeitsumfeld, attraktive Weiterbildungs- und Entwicklungsmöglichkeiten, eine bezahlte Mittagspause, ein Essenszuschuss und vieles mehr! https://www.uibk.ac.at/universitaet/zusatzleistungen/ . Für diese Position ist ein Entgelt von brutto € 690 / Monat (14 mal) * vorgesehen. * Stand 2026 Bewerbung: Wir freuen uns auf Ihre Onlinebewerbung bis 12.11.2026 unter Angabe der Chiffre REWI-16023 Kontakt: Bei Fragen zur Ausschreibung wenden Sie sich bitte an: Sabine Waibl Telefon: 004351250780202 E-Mail: sabine.waibl@uibk.ac.at Die Universität Innsbruck legt im Rahmen ihrer Personalpolitik Wert auf Chancengleichheit und Diversität. Die Universität Innsbruck strebt eine Erhöhung des Frauenanteils an und fordert daher qualifizierte Frauen ausdrücklich zur Bewerbung auf. Dies gilt insbesondere für Leitungsfunktionen sowie für wissenschaftliche Stellen. Bei Unterrepräsentation werden Frauen bei gleicher Qualifikation vorrangig aufgenommen. Die Universität Innsbruck trägt das Gütesiegel \"Wir sind inklusiv\". So laden wir qualifizierte Personen mit Behinderung und / oder chronischer Erkrankung ausdrücklich ein, sich zu bewerben. Zurück PDF Ausgabe Online bewerben teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail Universität Innsbruck Innrain 52 , Innsbruck Österreich Telefon: +43 512 507-0 Kontaktieren Sie uns Impressum Datenschutz Barrierefreiheit Zertifikate Powered by UniCMS | Webservices | zur Medizinischen Universität Innsbruck"
    },
    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=16007": {
      "title": "University Assistant (PhD position)",
      "description": "University Assistant (PhD position) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (PhD position) Start date/duration: as soon as possible for 4 years Administrative unit: Pharmacology and Toxicology Unit Extent of employment: 20 hours per week; will be increased to 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed Job Description: Your responsibilities: PhD in the field of experimental pharmacology Independent research in the following areas: Isolation and characterisation of primary cells, conducting animal studies using disease models, genome editing, gene expression and multi-omics analyses, molecular biology and biochemistry methods, FACS, histology, fluorescence microscopy and electrophysiology Contribution to organisational and administrative tasks Training and professional development, such as attending conferences and congresses, and undertaking further training Independent teaching and involvement in the teaching of pharmacology and toxicology Administrative duties Your profile: A completed Masters, Magister or Diplom degree in pharmacy or a related biomedical discipline Experience in one or more of the above-mentioned research areas Experience with animal experiments (FELASA certificate or equivalent qualification would be an advantage) Experience with human iPSC cultures and organoid models would be an advantage Teaching experience in pharmacology would be an advantage Very good written and spoken German and English An independent, structured and team-oriented approach to work Please include a written proposal outlining your doctoral research project with your application (max. 3 pages) Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/CHEM-PHARM-16007 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#dissertationsstellen Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for 20 hours per week amounts to € 1.888 per month (14 times)*. The salary will be increased to € 2.832 for 30 hours per week once the dissertation agreement has been signed and sent to the Personnel Department. The salary will be higher if you have worked in a similar position before. * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 12.11.2026 stating the code CHEM-PHARM-16007 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Univ.-Prof. Dr. Anouar BELKACEMI Phone: +4351258801 Email: pharmako-toxiko@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
    },
    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=15913": {
      "title": "University Assistant (postdoc)",
      "description": "University Assistant (postdoc) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (postdoc) Start date/duration: from 15.12.2026 for 4 years Administrative unit: Department of Urban Design and Land Use Planning Extent of employment: 40 hours per week Job Description: Your responsibilities: Conducting independent research in the field of landscape architecture, with a focus on biodigital design, within the framework of the Synthetic Landscape Lab is desirable Research-led teaching and supervision of undergraduate and postgraduate students (including co-supervision of dissertations within the department) Active involvement in the academic, organisational and administrative tasks of the research unit Supporting the strategic development and international visibility of the Synthetic Landscape Lab through publications, exhibitions, conferences and collaborative projects Contribution to the development and implementation of field research (particularly in Alpine regions) and to securing funding for international research collaborations Contributing to the development of new paradigms in landscape architecture in response to artificial intelligence, climate change and the loss of biodiversity Your profile: A completed PhD or doctoral degree in landscape architecture, architecture, urban planning or a closely related discipline Experience in academic research at the interface of synthetic landscapes, biodigital design, computational design and artificial intelligence Knowledge of integrating AI, biotechnology, scientific computation and complex systems thinking into architectural and landscape research, as well as into design processes, is desirable In-depth knowledge of the contemporary international discourse in architecture, landscape architecture and ecological design Experience with biological laboratory methods, computer-aided research, digital fabrication or other advanced experimental research methods is desirable Experience in field research, particularly in alpine environments, is desirable Teaching experience in a university context, as well as strong pedagogical and mentoring skills, is desirable Excellent digital literacy and advanced skills in computational methods, with a focus on contemporary design research Excellent command of English; as well as strong communication, organisational and teamwork skills, creativity and competence in interdisciplinary collaboration Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/ARCH-15913 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#post-doc Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for this position amounts to € 5.014 per month (14 times) * . * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 12.11.2026 stating the code ARCH-15913 Contact: If you have any questions about the tender, please contact: Institut für Städtebau Phone: ++43 512 507 64711 Email: ioud@uibk.ac.at The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
