    "https://lfuonline.uibk.ac.at/public/karriereportal.details?asg_id_in=16027": {
      "title": "University Assistant (postdoc) (substitute employee)",
      "description": "University Assistant (postdoc) Back PDF output Apply online University Assistant (postdoc) (substitute employee) Start date/duration: as soon as possible to 30.09.2030, but only until the return of the jobholder Administrative unit: Department of Accountancy, Taxation and Auditing Extent of employment: 32 hours per week Job Description: Your responsibilities: Delivering courses (in German and English) and supervising students Contributing to organisational and administrative tasks Research in the field of accounting Assisting with organisational and administrative tasks as well as evaluation activities Your profile: A completed doctoral/PhD degree in the social sciences or economics Relevant research experience in the following areas: financial accounting, sustainability reporting A number of high-quality publications commensurate with your academic seniority Additional research experience in the field of national accounting standards would be an advantage Excellent specialist knowledge in the following areas: financial accounting, sustainability reporting Methodological expertise in qualitative and/or quantitative methods Experience of using AI in research High-quality teaching experience in the fields of financial accounting and sustainability reporting Ability to teach in German and English International networks and experience of academic mobility Experience in securing external funding A research proposal must be submitted with the application Ability to work as part of a team Excellent communication skills Organisational skills Openness Euraxess: https://euraxess.ec.europa.eu/platforms/jobs/139/BWL-16027 The description associated with this job duties and requirements can be found at: https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/personalabteilung/wissenschaftliches_personal/profile/#post-doc Our offer: With us, you can expect exciting tasks, flexible working hours, a family-friendly working environment, attractive training and development opportunities, a paid lunch break, a meal allowance and much more! https://www.uibk.ac.at/en/career/additional-benefits/ . The minimum gross salary (stipulated by collective agreement) for this position amounts to € 4.011 per month (14 times) * . * as of 2026 Application: We are looking forward to receiving your online application by 13.11.2026 stating the code BWL-16027 The University of Innsbruck emphasizes equal opportunities and diversity in its personnel policy. The University of Innsbruck strives to increase the percentage of women and thus expressly encourages women to apply. This is particularely true for leading positions and scientific job offers. In case of underrepresentation women with the same qualifications will be given priority. The University of Innsbruck bears the \"We are inclusive\" seal of approval. We therefore expressly invite qualified individuals with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses to apply. Back PDF output Apply online teilen tweet mitteilen teilen mail"
